WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.330
In 2012, coal made about 40 per
cent of the UK's electricity.

2
00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.650
In 2024, Ratcliffe-on-Soar
power station closed,

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.750
and with it, British coal power ended.

4
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:18.710
In India, coal still made 71 per
cent of the electricity in 2025.

5
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:24.250
Yet per person, India emits 2.2
tonnes of carbon dioxide a year.

6
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.950
The UK emits 4.6.

7
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.430
So which country is managing
its energy sustainably?

8
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.150
In this mission, you'll compare
the two countries' energy mixes,

9
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.790
fuel by fuel, and their impacts.

10
00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.670
Then you'll fill in a scorecard
of progress and problems,

11
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.990
and judge each country.

12
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.990
Your mission: judge how sustainably Britain
and India are managing their energy.
